#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Rational exponents represent roots 🌱]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- $a^(m/n) = root(n, a^m)$ 🧮]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Example: $8^(1/3) = root(3, 8) = 2$ ✅]

#only("1")[
#voiceover("Let's quickly recap what we learned about rational exponents. Rational exponents are another way to represent roots.")
]

#only("2")[
#voiceover("The general form is a to the power of m over n equals the nth root of a to the power of m.")
]

#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, 8 to the power of one-third is the same as the cube root of 8, which equals 2.")
]
]

